  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Opposition leader Rahul Gandhi recently spoke at universities in the United States, including the University of Chicago and Columbia University, where he discussed topics ranging from Indian democracy and the national economy to the country's role in global affairs. Gandhi characterized the Indian state as being in a position of economic instability and criticized its perceived lack of influence on the international stage, specifically regarding trilateral diplomatic relations involving world leaders. These statements have drawn intense criticism from the Bharatiya Janata Party (BJP) and its allies, who accused him of tarnishing India's image on the global stage for political gain. Party officials and spokespersons labeled his rhetoric as contradictory to actual economic data and questioned his loyalty to the country. This exchange reflects an ongoing political debate regarding how domestic leadership and national progress should be represented by politicians when they are speaking to international audiences.",
